{title: Into Your Hand}
{subtitle: Psalms 31:5–6}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In your righteousness, deliver me
[C#]Turn your ear to me, [G#]come quick
[D#m]Be my rock of refuge now
A [C#]fortress that saves my [G#]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[B]You are my rock [C#]and stronghold
[B]Lead me for the [C#]sake of your name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Into your [C#]hand I commit [B]my spirit [C#]
[D#m]You have redeemed [C#]me, Lord
God [B]of truth, I trust in [C#]you
[D#m]Into your [C#]hand I commit [B]my spirit
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [B] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [C#] |
| [G#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D#m]Free me from the net they hid
For [C#]you are my refuge to[G#]day
[D#m]I hate worthless idols' cling
I [C#]put my trust in the [G#]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Into your [C#]hand I commit [B]my spirit [C#]
[D#m]You have redeemed [C#]me, Lord
God [B]of truth, I trust in [C#]you
[D#m]Into your [C#]hand I commit [B]my spirit [C#]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]You have seen my deep [C#]affliction
[D#m]Known the dis[F#]tress of my soul
[B]Not handed over to [C#]the enemy
[G#]You have set my feet [D#m][C#]free
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [B] | [C#] | [D#m] | [C#] |
| [B] | [C#] |

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]You have [C#]set my feet in [B]freedom [C#]
[D#m]I will re[C#]joice in [B]your mercy
{end_of_verse}
